# Run outputs are local by default -- see CLAUDE.md. Three exceptions:
# - results/reference/ holds the shared baseline and hqq_3bit runs every later stage is
#   defined relative to.
# - results/flipped/ holds the flipped-set JSON (Stage 3's deliverable) built from those two
#   runs -- Stage 4's search is evidence-driven, so its input has to be one shared file, not
#   whatever each of us happens to regenerate locally.
# - results/search_samples/ holds the FIXED seeded sample the search scores every candidate
#   on. The search's whole "not a corner cut" argument depends on every candidate seeing the
#   exact same questions; a sample redrawn per person would quietly break that even with the
#   same seed and size, if the flipped set it's drawn from ever drifts.
# All three are small text files, and having them in the repo lets the search, statistics and
# plotting work run without a GPU.
# NB: 'results/*' not 'results/', because git never descends into an excluded directory --
# with 'results/' the negations below would silently do nothing.
results/*
!results/reference/
!results/flipped/
!results/search_samples/
# Patch files (which modules each repair restores) and the per-module quantization-error ranking:
# small JSON, and every teammate's baseline runs must restore the identical module sets.
!results/patches/
!results/quant_error/
*.pt
*.safetensors
.env
wandb/
__pycache__/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

